<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Autorotate iOS entitlements.

  Keychain Sharing: the shared access group `codes.autorotate.shared` lets the
  iOS app, the macOS app and any extensions share managed secret items,
  connector admin credentials and the Infisical clientSecret
  (docs/architecture.md §5). Enable the "Keychain Sharing" capability in
  Xcode; Xcode will prefix the group with your App ID prefix automatically
  via $(AppIdentifierPrefix).

  App Group: `group.codes.autorotate` (added 2026-09-22 bundle-ID migration)
  is the shared container for UserDefaults / FileProvider coordination between
  the iOS and macOS companion apps. Enable the "App Groups" capability in
  Xcode; the group must be registered for every App ID that participates, so
  `codes.autorotate.ios` and `codes.autorotate.macos` need matching
  registrations on the owner side. See docs/rollouts/2026-09-22-bundle-id-migration.md.

  Associated Domains: `autorotate.codes` (added 2026-09-22 bundle-ID migration)
  powers Universal Links and shared web credentials. Enable the "Associated
  Domains" capability in Xcode; host the AASA at
  https://autorotate.codes/.well-known/apple-app-site-association (owner
  handles DNS + portal). Values below mirror the BotFleet convention:
  applinks for Universal Links, webcredentials for the shared Safari
  password flow.

  iCloud Keychain note: `kSecAttrSynchronizable` items (the "Sync via iCloud
  Keychain" toggle) require NO additional entitlement on iOS — sync happens
  "if allowed" by the user's iCloud settings, and KeychainManager falls back
  to device-local items otherwise. If Autorotate later adds its OWN iCloud
  container (e.g. for companion pairing state), add:

      <key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
      <array>
          <string>iCloud.com.autorotate.shared</string>
      </array>

  and enable the iCloud capability. It is intentionally absent today.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>keychain-access-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)codes.autorotate.shared</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.codes.autorotate</string>
    </array>
    <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
    <array>
        <string>applinks:autorotate.codes</string>
        <string>webcredentials:autorotate.codes</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>